  "notes": "Liability-classified SARs are remeasured to fair value each period, so the annual expense is the change in the cumulative accrued liability and is negative in Year 3 (-2,000) when fair value fell from $5.00 to $3.00. At December 31, Year 4 the year-end fair value of $6.00 equals the intrinsic value ($21 - $15), so the fully accrued liability of 48,000 exactly equals the 48,000 cash paid and the settlement entry records no gain or loss. Part d is satisfied: 4,000 + 16,000 - 2,000 + 30,000 = 48,000 = cash paid."
